      "output": "{\"verdict\":\"revise_required\",\"summary\":\"The diff genuinely deletes the dedicated recovery/reopen/rebind/continuation/replay machinery (-24k lines) and re-keys review flows, freshness, and acceptance on current materials and current-tree facts: accepted/checkpoint/review history is now read-only, publishAttempt no longer requires reopen/continuation permits, and verify-code/build-code fail closed on fresh authenticated test receipts, semantic integration reviews, and snapshot equivalence. Five stages, atomic create-only/CAS writers, human confirmations, separate close authorization, independent review facts vs permissions, and clean Runner/Skill release closure are preserved, and the repo is simpler rather than merely relocated (skills->runtime/review move fixes a real layering inversion enforced by new layering contracts). However, the final coverage record binds at least two acceptance criteria to oracles that do not plausibly exercise their predicates (AC-05 -> runner clean-install release tests; AC-07 -> progression-without-permits), and several fact/audit documents are internally inconsistent (gates 'passed' vs 'final coverage validator pending'; 14 files/65 tests claimed vs 6 files/25 tests recorded; empty diff_check evidence). Complexity hard gates are honestly reported but five budgets remain over limit.\",\"findings\":[{\"severity\":\"major\",\"path\":\"current-facts.json\",\"line\":114,\"issue\":\"AC-05 (independent review verdicts permanently preserved; unavailable required review => incomplete; serious findings need verified disposition or explicit risk authorization) is bound to oracle tests/integration/runner-clean-install.test.mjs, whose describe block and added tests cover Runner/Skill release closure and source hashing. Nothing in that oracle exercises review verdict preservation, unavailable-review incompleteness, or serious-finding disposition, so the 'covered' claim for AC-05 is not plausible.\",\"root_cause\":\"The final-coverage binding maps each AC to exactly one executed oracle but the validator (tools/architecture/verify-final-coverage.mjs) only checks that the oracle ran and passed, not that it exercises the AC's pass/fail predicates; a release-closure test was bound to a review-integrity criterion.\",\"recommendation\":\"Rebind AC-05 to an oracle that actually mutates review facts (e.g. the revise_required/unavailable/serious-finding guards in tests/final-cutover-guards.red.test.mjs or tests/stage-risk-acceptance.test.mjs), record the fresh hash-bound execution, and rerun the coverage validator in final mode.\"},{\"severity\":\"major\",\"path\":\"current-facts.json\",\"line\":138,\"issue\":\"AC-07 (deletions completed as vertical slices: entry points, implementation, contracts, samples, dedicated tests and terminology gone together; replacement path passes; zeroed list all 0) is bound to oracle tests/integration/progression-without-permits.test.mjs, whose four tests only prove permit-free continuation after material revision, checkpoint read-only history, and stale-fact handling. It contains no deleted-entry unreachability, orphan-reference, or silent-fallback negative oracle for the deleted recovery/replay slices.\",\"root_cause\":\"Same single-oracle mapping gap as AC-05: a progression test was cited for a deletion-slice criterion because it passed in the same targeted matrix, not because it verifies deletion semantics.\",\"recommendation\":\"Bind AC-07 to the oracle(s) that assert old entry points fail and retired symbols/paths are zero (tests/contract/runtime-facade.test.mjs invalidate-run rejection, tests/contract/legacy-zero.test.mjs, repository-inventory hard-zero gates), or add a dedicated negative-oracle test for the deleted slices and re-execute the matrix.\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"path\":\"current-facts.json\",\"line\":49,\"issue\":\"final_gates.status is 'passed' with missing_required_commands empty, yet summary.formal_status says 'current-tree facts bound; final coverage validator pending'. A passed terminal gate that simultaneously declares its own coverage validation pending is self-contradictory.\",\"root_cause\":\"The summary string was not regenerated after the final coverage validation completed (or the gates record was assembled before the coverage run and the status field was flipped independently).\",\"recommendation\":\"Regenerate the final-gates record so status and summary agree; if the coverage validator has not actually run against this tree, downgrade status to incomplete per validateFinalGates.\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"path\":\"docs/architecture/final-coverage-audit.md\",\"line\":7,\"issue\":\"The audit doc states 'The current targeted execution ran 14 test files / 65 tests and passed', but current-facts.json focused_final records 6 test files / 25 tests for the same final targeted matrix. The human-readable audit disagrees with the hash-bound machine record it describes.\",\"root_cause\":\"The markdown audit was hand-updated (or copied from an earlier larger matrix run) after the final 6-file focused matrix was recorded, reintroducing the drift the v2 machine-bound design was meant to eliminate.\",\"recommendation\":\"Derive the counts in final-coverage-audit.md from evidence/phase-9/focused-final-current-facts.json (and any additional archived matrices with explicit refs), or correct the sentence to the recorded 6 files / 25 tests.\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"path\":\"current-facts.json\",\"line\":43,\"issue\":\"The diff_check final-gate evidence has sha256 e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855, the hash of the empty string: the archived diff-check output for a 24k-line deletion diff is an empty file. As supplied, the gate proves only that an empty artifact exists, not what was diffed or checked.\",\"root_cause\":\"The diff-check command apparently emits nothing on success, so the hash-bound archived output carries no observable content about the compared trees.\",\"recommendation\":\"Make the diff-check emit a non-empty summary (compared tree hashes and verdict) so the archived evidence is self-describing, or document in the gates record that empty output is the success contract.\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"path\":\"runtime/review/canonical-review-result.mjs\",\"line\":167,\"issue\":\"authenticateCanonicalReviewResult now collapses provider_attempts to the terminal completed attempt per provider before authenticating outputs; a superseded completed attempt whose output record is missing or misbound no longer raises 'completed provider output is missing or misbound'. Corruption or misbinding in non-terminal attempts is silently tolerated.\",\"root_cause\":\"The terminalProviderAttempts pre-pass drops earlier completed attempts from the authentication loop instead of only from verdict aggregation.\",\"recommendation\":\"Keep terminal-attempt selection for aggregation, but still validate that every completed provider attempt has a present, correctly bound output record (or explicitly document and test that superseded attempts are exempt).\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"path\":\"core/task-handle.mjs\",\"line\":924,\"issue\":\"openTask no longer authenticates target-repo-root migration lineage (validateTargetRepoRootMigration deleted) and validateManifest now accepts execution_mode 'legacy_pinned' with no runner_root/runner_oid coherence checks, while migrateTaskTargetRepoRoot and the target_repo_root_migration manifest pointer remain writable. New migration records can still be created but their chain, integrity hash, and repository identity are never verified on open, so a forged or corrupted lineage goes undetected.\",\"root_cause\":\"The on-open lineage verifiers were removed together with the runner recovery machinery, but the target-repo-root migration writer and manifest fields were retained as a half-supported mechanism.\",\"recommendation\":\"Either keep a minimal read-side integrity check (pointer ref/hash and record schema) for the retained migration writer, or finish the slice by removing the target-repo-root migration writer and manifest pointer so no unverified mutable lineage remains.\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"path\":\"workflows/verify-code/skill-deps.yaml\",\"line\":3,\"issue\":\"The verify-code stage skill closure now declares only wh-review; the conditional isolated-browser-qa, test-strategy, and resolving-merge-conflicts skills were removed and the v3 SKILL.md drops the browser-QA evidence path and the six-action close runbook, while the runtime still accepts facts.browser_qa and task-close still implements the six-action confirmed close. UI acceptance evidence has no declared stage skill anymore.\",\"root_cause\":\"Skill-declaration simplification outpaced the retained runtime surfaces: browser_qa remained an allowed verify-code fact and close remains a six-action executor, but the workflow no longer declares the skills that produce/consume them.\",\"recommendation\":\"Either re-declare isolated-browser-qa (and close-conflict skill) as conditional verify-code skills, or remove browser_qa from the verify-code facts contract and state explicitly in the SKILL that UI acceptance is out of scope for the stage.\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"path\":\"docs/architecture/final-complexity-report.json\",\"line\":null,\"issue\":\"Five published budgets remain over limit (formal_test_lines 25057 vs limit 12000, production_lines 29967 vs 15000, schemas 36 vs 10, persistent_object_families 10 vs 5, largest_core_file_lines 2975 vs 1000) and focused/full test seconds actuals are null. Reporting is honest and reproducible, but the 'deeply simplified' outcome is only partially achieved and the duration budgets are unmeasured.\",\"root_cause\":\"The final report correctly embeds the full buildReport() payload, but the follow-up reductions and duration measurements were deferred rather than completed before the final gate.\",\"recommendation\":\"Keep the hard gates as-is (they are zero), but either close or explicitly schedule the remaining budget deltas and record actual focused/full test durations so AC-14's actual/target/limit/delta/plan data is complete.\"}]}"
