      "output": "{\"verdict\":\"revise_required\",\"summary\":\"The recovery/reopen/rebind/replay vertical slice is genuinely removed rather than relocated: core/task-recovery.mjs (471), scripts/task-recovery.mjs (1741), core/build-spec-receipt-recovery.mjs (456), scripts/validate-stage-replay.mjs (244), tools/cli/task-migrate-runner-root.mjs, the recovery credential/generation schemas, the reopen/rebind provenance schema fields, and six dedicated recovery/bridge test files are all deleted, with a filesystem existsSync-based task-only-governance zero gate and an explicit negative test for retired invalidation record paths guarding regrowth. Formal safety is strengthened in places: requireFinalIntegrationReview and certifyBuildCodeQualityBasis now throw unless a completed semantic review carries verdict==='pass' or resolution_verified===true; selectReviewRound returns none/phase_quality_fact_recorded rather than chasing verdicts to pass; authenticatedImplementationChanged adds --no-renames and verifies untracked blob_oid via git hash-object; the three-writer atomic fault contract is preserved and stated more precisely as {applies, reason}; the runtime/review relocation is pinned by two new layering contract tests including a Tarjan SCC check. However the change set removes or dilutes several quality oracles rather than preserving their semantics under simpler behavior, and the supplied current facts do not bind the acceptance criteria they claim to cover. AC-12 requires that every tracked test carry exactly one disposition, yet the disposition ledger, its generator, and its contract test are all deleted with no replacement enumerator. tools/architecture/inventory.mjs now unconditionally requires docs/architecture/deletions-proof.json under --check, but that artifact appears in neither the 143-file diff nor the inventory ledger, so the gate the diff adds cannot pass and AC-06's per-deletion proof is unverifiable from the frozen bundle. The AC-11 runner-drift fail-closed check is deleted and its test inverted to expect success. The claimed-vs-actual diff equality check is now skipped whenever the claim list is empty, which prose actual_changes reliably produces. These are oracle removals on the safety side of the ledger, so the simplification is not yet demonstrably quality-preserving.\",\"findings\":[{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"path\":\"tools/architecture/inventory.mjs\",\"line\":null,\"issue\":\"validateDeletionProof() requires docs/architecture/deletions-proof.json (schema workflowhub-deletions-proof.v1, 40-hex baseline commit/tree, per-entry absent===true, consumer_zero_ref into complexity-baseline.json#/hard_gates/dedicated_recovery_state, an existing replacement_oracle, and user_confirmation.ref === docs/architecture/legacy-import-proof.json with confirmation.user_confirmed === true), and main() pushes its errors on every --check run. That file is present in neither the 143-file diff-summary.txt nor any docs/architecture/repository-inventory.tsv hunk, so inventory --check reports 'deletions proof is missing' and AC-06's per-deletion proof cannot be verified from the frozen bundle.\",\"root_cause\":\"A new hard gate was added in the same change that deletes the old deletion-proof tooling (tools/architecture/deletion-proof.mjs, tests/contract/deletion-proof.test.mjs), but the data artifact the new gate consumes was not included in the reviewed change set or the inventory ledger.\",\"recommendation\":\"Add docs/architecture/deletions-proof.json to the change set with an inventory row and a disposition, or make validateDeletionProof() the only gate that can satisfy AC-06 and prove it green by including it in the focused-final command set. Either way the frozen bundle must contain the artifact its own gate requires.\"},{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"path\":\"docs/architecture/test-disposition.tsv\",\"line\":null,\"issue\":\"AC-12's pass condition requires that every tracked test carry exactly one disposition. This change deletes the ledger (docs/architecture/test-disposition.tsv, 159 lines), its generator (tools/architecture/test-disposition.mjs, 90 lines), and its contract test (tests/contract/test-disposition.test.mjs, 53 lines) — including the assertions that rejected duplicate rows and non-keep rows lacking a replacement oracle, and that protected behavioral oracles stay 'keep'. current-facts.json maps AC-12 to tests/integration/mutation-guards.test.mjs, the same oracle already bound to AC-04, which validates writer mutation guards and cannot enumerate tracked-test dispositions.\",\"root_cause\":\"Disposition tracking was classified as task-only governance and deleted alongside the recovery slice, but AC-12 still depends on it and no replacement enumerator was introduced; the coverage map was patched by pointing AC-12 at an unrelated existing test.\",\"recommendation\":\"Either restore a tracked-test disposition enumerator (it can be far simpler than the deleted TSV pipeline — a single contract test that walks git ls-files for test paths and asserts each has exactly one recorded disposition) or obtain explicit agreement to amend AC-12. Do not leave AC-12 bound to mutation-guards.test.mjs, which cannot fail for the reason AC-12 describes.\"},{\"severity\":\"major\",\"path\":\"core/stage-context.mjs\",\"line\":null,\"issue\":\"The runner-drift fail-closed check is removed: the guarded call `if (taskHandle.manifest.runner_root !== undefined) assertTaskRunnerIdentity(taskHandle, { runnerRoot, stage: normalizedStage })` is deleted, and core/__tests__/stage-context.test.mjs is inverted from `expect(() => bootstrapStage(...)).toThrow(/runner identity mismatch/i)` to a passing test named 'sidecar mode ignores a legacy pinned runner when opening the current stage'. AC-11 requires fail-loud behavior on a missing or mismatched Runner; a task whose manifest pins a runner_root that no longer matches the runner now opens the stage silently.\",\"root_cause\":\"Removing runner rebinding machinery also removed the drift detection that made a stale pinned runner_root loud, and the test was rewritten to assert the new tolerant behavior instead of relocating the guard to the sidecar resolution path.\",\"recommendation\":\"Keep sidecar resolution simple but restore a loud signal: when manifest.runner_root is present and does not resolve to the active runner, throw (or require an explicit ignore intent) rather than silently proceeding, and restore a test asserting the mismatch is rejected. Confirm which oracle now covers AC-11's mismatched-Runner case, since runner-clean-install.test.mjs exercises distribution, not per-task pin drift.\"},{\"severity\":\"major\",\"path\":\"core/stage-handlers.mjs\",\"line\":null,\"issue\":\"The claimed-vs-actual diff equality check is now conditional: `if (claimedChanges.length > 0 && !sameStringSet(...))`. Combined with `return pathOnlyCompletionClaim(actual_changes) ? paths : []`, any prose actual_changes yields zero claims and the equality check is skipped entirely, so a completion whose tasks.md narrative contradicts the authenticated diff certifies. The inline comment states the implementation receipt is authoritative, but certifyBuildCodeQualityBasis does not require a path-only claim, so the stricter branch is optional at the author's discretion.\",\"root_cause\":\"The bypass was introduced to tolerate descriptive task notes, but it was implemented as an unconditional skip rather than as a requirement that the authoritative receipt supply the paths when the claim is non-enumerable.\",\"recommendation\":\"Do not let claim shape select the strictness level. When actual_changes is not path-only, derive the claim set from the authenticated implementation receipt and compare that against changedFiles, so the equality invariant holds for every completion. Add a red test where prose actual_changes accompanies a mismatched diff and assert it fails closed.\"},{\"severity\":\"major\",\"path\":\"tests/stage-interaction-contract.test.mjs\",\"line\":null,\"issue\":\"The interaction/documentation oracle is reduced to phrase matching — `expect(skill, stage).toMatch(/current (?:four )?materials/i)` and `expect(skill, stage).toMatch(/audit/i)` plus two build-code/verify-code phrase checks — and three behavioral tests are deleted (human briefs and verify repair handoff; host-visible interaction, component facts and handoff; make-decision talk and grill outcomes), a net -214 lines. AC-09 and AC-15 require that documentation not contradict actual behavior; a SKILL.md containing the word 'audit' now satisfies the contract regardless of whether the described confirmation and handoff surfaces exist.\",\"root_cause\":\"SKILL.md files were heavily rewritten (build-code -487, build-plan -347, build-spec -473, make-decision -501, verify-code -507 lines) and the contract test was relaxed to phrase presence so it would pass against the new prose, instead of re-expressing the behavioral assertions against the new text.\",\"recommendation\":\"Restore assertions that tie each stage's documented interaction surface to a behavior that exists in code (confirmation boundary, handoff artifact, human brief), even if expressed more compactly than before. Phrase-presence matching cannot detect the doc/behavior contradiction AC-15 targets.\"},{\"severity\":\"major\",\"path\":\"bundle/current-facts.json\",\"line\":null,\"issue\":\"The AC-to-oracle mapping does not support the 'covered' claims. AC-05 (independent review facts and serious findings never rewritten; unavailable facts ⇒ incomplete) is bound to tests/integration/runner-clean-install.test.mjs, which audits distribution cleanliness and cannot exercise review-fact independence. AC-06, AC-08, AC-13 and AC-14 all share tests/contract/repository-inventory.test.mjs. AC-12 shares AC-04's mutation-guards.test.mjs. Several oracles' execution refs point at evidence/phase-9/final-targeted-matrix.json or repository-inventory-current.json rather than the 6-file focused-final run (25 tests, 25 passed) that is the only executed evidence supplied.\",\"root_cause\":\"Coverage was recorded by assigning each AC to a surviving test file after deletions rather than by identifying which test can actually fail for that AC's reason, so oracle identity was lost during the consolidation.\",\"recommendation\":\"Rebind each AC to an oracle that fails when that AC is violated, and show it in an executed run. AC-05 in particular needs an oracle over review-fact immutability and the unavailable-facts ⇒ incomplete path; the strengthened requireFinalIntegrationReview and certifyBuildCodeQualityBasis review checks are the natural subjects, and the new red test in tests/final-cutover-guards.red.test.mjs ('does not certify build-code completion from revise_required without a verified resolution') is a candidate that is not currently cited.\"},{\"severity\":\"major\",\"path\":\"core/task-handle.mjs\",\"line\":null,\"issue\":\"listCanonicalPhaseTraceRefs replaces hard failures with silent skips: invalid phase directory names and non-hex snapshot directory names now `continue` instead of throwing, the tolerateHistoricalInvalidRecords option is removed, and the invalid-trace-record throw is deleted. AC-07 names silent fallback (静默 fallback) as an explicit failure condition. A malformed or truncated trace record is now indistinguishable from an absent one, so a phase whose trace exists but is unreadable enumerates as having no trace and downstream 'missing facts ⇒ incomplete' logic reports the wrong reason.\",\"root_cause\":\"Historical records must remain readable without blocking continuation, and skipping was the simplest way to stop them from throwing; but the skip was applied to malformed current records as well, converting a corruption signal into silence.\",\"recommendation\":\"Distinguish 'historical and non-replayable' from 'malformed'. Skip only records outside the current snapshot; for the current snapshot_tree, throw with the offending path so corruption remains loud. Add a test that a malformed trace record under the current snapshot fails closed while a historical one is skipped.\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"path\":\"docs/architecture/repository-inventory.tsv\",\"line\":null,\"issue\":\"The inventory ledger and the frozen diff disagree on the tracked file set. Rows are removed for core/__tests__/task-runner-root-migration.test.mjs, core/__tests__/task-target-repo-migration.test.mjs and tests/design-stage-skill-order.red.test.mjs, and a row is added for tests/integration/execution-snapshot-isolation.test.mjs, but none of these four paths appear in diff-summary.txt's 143-file list as added or deleted. Rows for evidence/phase-5/*, evidence/phase-7/*, evidence/phase-9/final-coverage.json and evidence/phase-9/final-gates.json are also removed while current-facts.json still cites evidence/phase-9 artifacts as execution refs.\",\"root_cause\":\"The inventory was regenerated against a working tree that differs from the tree the diff was cut against, so ledger edits reflect file operations that the reviewed change set does not contain.\",\"recommendation\":\"Regenerate the inventory against the frozen snapshot_tree and reconcile: either include the four file additions/deletions in the change set or restore their rows. Also keep ledger rows for any evidence path that current-facts.json cites, otherwise the cited execution refs are unlocatable from the inventory.\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"path\":\"bundle/current-facts.json\",\"line\":null,\"issue\":\"The gate status is self-contradicting: final_gates.status is 'passed' with all seven required commands listed, while summary.formal_status reads 'current-tree facts bound; final coverage validator pending'. tests/contract/final-coverage.test.mjs and tools/architecture/verify-final-coverage.mjs are both modified in this change set, so the pending validator is the one whose behavior changed.\",\"root_cause\":\"The facts snapshot was assembled before the final coverage validator finished running, and the aggregate status field was set independently of the per-area summary.\",\"recommendation\":\"Run the final coverage validator against the frozen tree and make status and formal_status agree. A 'passed' aggregate that carries a 'pending' sub-status cannot be relied on as the fresh-facts basis the invariants require for formal publish.\"}]}"
